# The versions of the software clanker-learn puts into its projects: Claude Code and the
# editor (code-server). Each is fetched once, at this version, by a throwaway container, into
# a distribution on the data volume, which projects get their copy from.
#
# This file is the repository's baseline and is part of the image (/opt/cl/versions.env).
# /data/versions.local.env overrides it key by key: Refresh (Settings -> Software, or
# `cl agent refresh` / `cl editor refresh`) raises a version there, never here and never
# down, and "Use repo version" takes that key out again.
#
# One KEY=VALUE a line; a version is digits and dots only. CLAUDE_CODE_EXT_VERSION is Claude
# Code's editor extension (Open VSX), bundled into its distribution and refreshed with it.
CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION=2.1.330
CODE_SERVER_VERSION=4.126.0
CLAUDE_CODE_EXT_VERSION=2.1.330
